---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHero from '../../components/PageHero.astro';
import Section from '../../components/Section.astro';
import Quote from '../../components/Quote.astro';
import Card from '../../components/Card.astro';
import { sevaOpportunities } from '../../data/site';

const howToHelp = [
  'Help as much as you can.',
  'Help as efficiently as you can.',
  'Help as silently as you can.',
  'Help as lovingly as you can.',
];
---

<Base
  title="Seva"
  description="Seva at the center is a spiritual practice — recognising the Divine in all beings and serving them. Regular and special service projects, and how to take part."
>
  <PageHero
    eyebrow="Seva"
    title="Service as a spiritual practice"
    lede="Service at the Sai Baba Center is primarily a spiritual practice, aimed at elevating us through constant practice to recognise the Divinity in all beings."
    image="/img/seva/paper-cranes.webp"
  />

  <Section width="narrow">
    <div class="rich reveal">
      <h2>What is seva?</h2>
      <p>
        As Swami says, <em>“The best way to please me is to see Me in all beings and serve them just as you would like
        to serve Me.”</em>
      </p>
      <p>
        Swami also teaches that before engaging in seva — selfless service — one must attain purity of heart. It is
        important to examine one’s motives, skills, intentions and qualifications, and to be aware of the desire for
        fame or egoism. To truly serve, one must relinquish pride, status, wealth, scholarship and position, and
        instead practise humility, obedience, discipline and compassion.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="reveal mt-10 rounded-2xl bg-indigo-ink-900 p-8">
      <h3 class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold !text-white">How can we help?</h3>
      <ul class="mt-5 grid gap-3 sm:grid-cols-2">
        {
          howToHelp.map((line) => (
            <li class="flex items-center gap-3 rounded-xl bg-white/5 px-4 py-3 text-indigo-ink-100">
              <span class="h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-saffron-400" />
              {line}
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ul>
      <p class="mt-5 text-indigo-ink-200">Leave the rest to God, who gave you the chance to serve.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="rich reveal mt-12">
      <h2>Why join a group service project?</h2>
      <p>
        Swami says, <em>“What a single individual cannot accomplish, a well-knit group or society can achieve. A man
        walking alone will feel tired and miserable at the end of five miles, but walking with a group would find the
        five miles a happy jaunt. He arrives refreshed and strong.”</em>
      </p>
      <p>
        Our projects are designed to meet the diverse needs and abilities of participants. If none of these projects
        address your specific areas of interest, please contact the seva coordinator to find a suitable opportunity.
      </p>
    </div>
  </Section>

  <Section width="narrow" tone="sand">
    <Quote>
      God will not ask you what seva did you do? He will ask, with what motive did you do it? What was the intention
      that prompted it? You may weigh the seva and boast of its quantity, but God seeks the quality and holiness of the
      heart and the purity of the mind.
    </Quote>
  </Section>

  <Section
    eyebrow="Get involved"
    title="Standing seva opportunities"
    lede="These run on a fixed rhythm through the year. To join any of them, talk to your child’s teacher."
  >
    <div class="grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-2">
      {
        sevaOpportunities.map((opportunity) => (
          <article class="reveal flex flex-col rounded-2xl bg-white p-7 ring-1 ring-sand-200">
            <p class="text-[0.68rem] font-semibold tracking-[0.14em] text-saffron-700 uppercase">{opportunity.when}</p>
            <h3 class="mt-2 font-display text-2xl font-semibold">{opportunity.title}</h3>
            <p class="mt-3 flex-1 leading-relaxed text-ink-700">{opportunity.body}</p>
            {opportunity.href && (
              <a
                href={opportunity.href}
                class="mt-5 inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-sm font-semibold text-saffron-700 hover:text-saffron-600"
              >
                More about this seva
                <svg class="h-3.5 w-3.5" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none" aria-hidden="true">
                  <path d="M2 7h10m0 0L8 3m4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" />
                </svg>
              </a>
            )}
          </article>
        ))
      }
    </div>
  </Section>

  <Section tone="sand" eyebrow="Through the year" title="Special service projects">
    <div class="grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-3">
      <Card title="UNICEF Trick-or-Treat" eyebrow="October">
        Bal Vikas students trick-or-treat as UNICEF volunteers to support children’s causes worldwide.
      </Card>
      <Card title="Birthday Care Kits" eyebrow="November">
        Devotees assemble care kits for the homeless in Dallas to help them through the winter. Distributed by senior
        Bal Vikas students, they include handmade hats and scarves created by the children themselves.
      </Card>
      <Card title="Thanksgiving Meals-on-Wheels" eyebrow="November">
        Families deliver meals to the elderly, lonely and homebound on the holiday, in a project organised by the local
        Visiting Nurses Association.
      </Card>
    </div>

    <h3 class="reveal mt-14 font-display text-2xl font-semibold">Regular projects</h3>
    <div class="mt-6 grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4">
      <Card title="Austin Street Center" href="/seva/narayana-seva/">
        A wholesome, home-cooked vegetarian meal served on the first Friday of every month.
      </Card>
      <Card title="Park Cleaning">
        Students clean parks and streams in Plano.
      </Card>
      <Card title="Feed My Starving Children">
        Children and their families take part in packing meals.
      </Card>
      <Card title="Nursing homes">
        Children visit elderly residents to play games, sing songs, make crafts and share their love. Holidays and
        birthdays are specially planned to make our elderly friends feel remembered.
      </Card>
    </div>
  </Section>
</Base>
